This assert statement checks if the value of x increases by y in the function, where RET represents the return value of the function "Sum".
```cs
public static int Sum(int x, int y)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < y; i++){
        x.Inc(1);
    }
    // @@@ Value of x increases by y in the function
    return x;
}
```
In the provided code, x increases by y because the for loop inside the Sum function causes x to increment by 1 for each iteration from 0 to y-1. Thus, the assert statement checks if the value of x increased by y in the function.--------------------```cs
